1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:01,410
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,410 --> 00:00:03,340
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,340 --> 00:00:05,210
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:07,110 --> 00:00:08,210
(Episode 11)

5
00:01:17,980 --> 00:01:19,050
Who's in there?

6
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:41,610
Come out. Now.

7
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:45,640
I said, come out.

8
00:02:13,610 --> 00:02:14,610
Mr. Seo.

9
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:17,040
Chief Cha?

10
00:02:17,540 --> 00:02:19,610
What brings you here at this hour?

11
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:22,350
I thought I saw a woman
come in here.

12
00:02:23,150 --> 00:02:24,150
What's this?

13
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:28,950
You must be tired
if you're seeing things like that.

14
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:31,320
What do you mean by that?

15
00:02:41,070 --> 00:02:42,070
Oh, not again.

16
00:02:43,030 --> 00:02:45,040
Old book dust sets off my allergies.

17
00:02:46,970 --> 00:02:48,910
No, face that way. Look that way.

18
00:02:49,770 --> 00:02:50,780
You have something on your...

19
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:52,940
Get away. Don't.

20
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:55,410
I'll share what I find
sometime next week.

21
00:03:06,460 --> 00:03:07,930
Are you all right, Attorney Seo?

22
00:03:08,660 --> 00:03:11,130
I'm fine. What about you, Eun Seol?

23
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:14,030
I'm good. I'm sorry about this.

24
00:03:14,100 --> 00:03:15,830
I should've been more careful.

25
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:17,400
No, it's fine.

26
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:20,100
My hunch was right.

27
00:03:21,110 --> 00:03:22,840
I thought Chief Cha was suspicious.

28
00:03:24,880 --> 00:03:26,780
Wait, what's his name?

29
00:03:27,050 --> 00:03:28,110
Cha Seok Jin.

30
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:34,090
Why? Do you know him?

31
00:03:36,190 --> 00:03:37,190
A little.

32
00:03:43,830 --> 00:03:44,830
Where were you?

33
00:03:45,730 --> 00:03:46,930
Just down in the archives.

34
00:03:47,670 --> 00:03:49,030
What's this? Didn't you go home?

35
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:52,840
I brought a late-night snack
so we could have a little date.

36
00:03:53,670 --> 00:03:54,670
Sit down. Come on.

37
00:03:55,740 --> 00:03:56,740
You're something else.

38
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:01,380
Even I have to admit
I'm one of a kind.

39
00:04:01,550 --> 00:04:04,850
Guys are lining up for me,
but I'm completely hooked on you.

40
00:04:07,250 --> 00:04:10,020
Do you know
when I first fell for you?

41
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:13,390
- When?
- The first day I saw you.

42
00:04:14,130 --> 00:04:17,760
On my seventh birthday,
you walked in with your parents,

43
00:04:17,830 --> 00:04:19,460
and it looked like you were glowing.

44
00:04:20,100 --> 00:04:21,100
Glowing, really?

45
00:04:21,900 --> 00:04:23,530
I've been head over heels for you
ever since,

46
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:25,940
so I haven't even looked
at another guy.

47
00:04:29,740 --> 00:04:31,410
When did you start to like me?

48
00:04:33,910 --> 00:04:35,950
Come on, why are you asking
something so cheesy?

49
00:04:36,650 --> 00:04:39,250
Just tell me anyway.
When did you start liking me?

50
00:04:41,620 --> 00:04:43,450
I don't know. I don't remember.

51
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:47,260
Are you really going
to be like this?

52
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,200
The jokbal is delicious.
Go ahead. I mean...

53
00:04:57,340 --> 00:04:59,900
All right. Okay, fine.

54
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:01,840
Here, say "ah."

55
00:05:05,810 --> 00:05:07,450
Look. See my hand shaking?

56
00:05:08,180 --> 00:05:09,250
Come on.

57
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:13,950
I'll give you a pass again
this time.

58
00:05:19,620 --> 00:05:20,630
It's good, right?

59
00:05:20,990 --> 00:05:22,390
- Eat up.
- Sure.

60
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:25,060
Toss these noodles for me.

61
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:28,600
Why aren't you home yet?

62
00:05:30,370 --> 00:05:32,340
Okay. Come home soon.

63
00:05:34,270 --> 00:05:36,070
Is she really that into Seok Jin?

64
00:05:37,340 --> 00:05:39,180
Is she with Chief Cha?

65
00:05:39,810 --> 00:05:42,880
Yes. They're having
a late-night snack at the office.

66
00:05:45,380 --> 00:05:46,680
Ma'am,

67
00:05:47,420 --> 00:05:50,090
what do you think of Chief Cha
as a son-in-law?

68
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:52,790
I'm torn.

69
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:54,690
Hae Ra likes him so much,

70
00:05:54,760 --> 00:05:56,760
so a part of me wants them
to be together.

71
00:05:57,500 --> 00:05:59,000
But my husband's against it,

72
00:05:59,060 --> 00:06:01,200
so I wonder
if I should side with him.

73
00:06:02,130 --> 00:06:03,500
What do you think?

74
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:08,210
In my opinion,

75
00:06:08,970 --> 00:06:12,040
having overly powerful in-laws
is a double-edged sword.

76
00:06:12,510 --> 00:06:14,150
A double-edged sword?

77
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:18,150
Having powerful in-laws
like Assemblyman Oh's family...

78
00:06:18,150 --> 00:06:19,420
might feel reassuring at first.

79
00:06:19,850 --> 00:06:22,290
But once Hae Ra inherits Cheongma,

80
00:06:22,420 --> 00:06:24,120
do you really think her in-laws
will just sit back?

81
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:26,360
In exchange for protecting her,

82
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:28,230
they'll act like they own the place.

83
00:06:28,490 --> 00:06:31,130
How could Hae Ra possibly
stand up to them?

84
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:34,500
I suppose that's just human nature.

85
00:06:35,330 --> 00:06:38,240
When you put it that way,
maybe Seok Jin is the right choice.

86
00:06:38,670 --> 00:06:40,710
He doesn't have a family
to back him up,

87
00:06:40,970 --> 00:06:42,770
so he'll be loyal to Cheongma.

88
00:06:43,610 --> 00:06:45,310
If he supports Hae Ra well,

89
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:47,710
you couldn't ask
for a better husband.

90
00:06:48,710 --> 00:06:52,050
I doubt my husband
will ever see it that way.

91
00:06:52,150 --> 00:06:54,690
Take your time
and try to persuade him.

92
00:06:55,490 --> 00:06:57,460
They say parents can never win
against their children.

93
00:06:57,460 --> 00:07:00,090
With you in Hae Ra's corner,
what's there to worry about?

94
00:07:01,660 --> 00:07:03,130
At times,

95
00:07:03,360 --> 00:07:05,830
you seem to care more
for Hae Ra than I do.

96
00:07:07,470 --> 00:07:08,870
That's nonsense.

97
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:11,400
Then again,

98
00:07:11,470 --> 00:07:13,470
from her formula to her diapers,

99
00:07:13,740 --> 00:07:16,370
you were the one who fed,
bathed, and raised her,

100
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:17,680
so it makes sense.

101
00:07:22,950 --> 00:07:24,150
Is Hae Ra still not home?

102
00:07:25,650 --> 00:07:27,390
She said she'll be home soon.

103
00:07:27,590 --> 00:07:28,720
Where is she?

104
00:07:29,390 --> 00:07:30,390
Well...

105
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:33,060
She's with Seok Jin.

106
00:07:34,930 --> 00:07:36,190
This late at night?

107
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:40,030
You need to keep
a better eye on Hae Ra.

108
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:42,370
It'll be a problem
if she crosses any lines.

109
00:07:46,570 --> 00:07:49,740
See? We have a long way to go.

110
00:07:56,310 --> 00:08:00,350
(Cheongchun Gositel)

111
00:08:01,790 --> 00:08:04,420
So? Have you decided on
a concept for the competition?

112
00:08:04,890 --> 00:08:07,930
Yes, all the research I did
really helped.

113
00:08:08,630 --> 00:08:09,930
I'm glad to hear that.

114
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:12,800
By the way,

115
00:08:14,100 --> 00:08:16,830
my sister invited you over
for dinner.

116
00:08:16,900 --> 00:08:18,000
How about tomorrow evening?

117
00:08:18,740 --> 00:08:20,270
Tomorrow evening?

118
00:08:21,110 --> 00:08:23,270
If you're free,
have dinner at our place tomorrow.

119
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:25,540
That day...

120
00:08:25,740 --> 00:08:29,110
I think my sister felt terrible
after seeing you leave like that.

121
00:08:31,280 --> 00:08:32,720
This really isn't necessary.

122
00:08:34,190 --> 00:08:36,650
But okay. I'll be there.

123
00:08:43,730 --> 00:08:47,030
Anyway, how do you know Chief Cha?

124
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:49,630
He was a few grades above me
in high school.

125
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:51,800
Were you close?

126
00:08:52,900 --> 00:08:54,010
Why do you ask?

127
00:08:54,640 --> 00:08:57,510
Chief Cha is also a judge
for this competition.

128
00:08:57,910 --> 00:08:59,710
I was thinking you could ask him
for a favor.

129
00:09:03,980 --> 00:09:04,980
What is it?

130
00:09:05,180 --> 00:09:07,220
You don't want to
because it feels like cheating?

131
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:12,120
It's not that.
I'm not in a position to be picky.

132
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:14,230
But?

133
00:09:15,860 --> 00:09:18,060
I just don't think
it would do any good.

134
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:19,930
Truth is,

135
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:21,900
he doesn't like me.

136
00:09:24,800 --> 00:09:26,640
Thank you for the ride home.

137
00:09:28,610 --> 00:09:30,170
I'll take that.

138
00:09:30,510 --> 00:09:31,640
No, I've got it.

139
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:33,950
- Okay.
- Right.

140
00:09:36,280 --> 00:09:37,350
Watch out.

141
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:39,120
I'm sorry.

142
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:41,420
- Are you okay?
- I'm okay.

143
00:09:42,250 --> 00:09:43,250
Night, then.

144
00:10:23,330 --> 00:10:26,500
I'm sorry about this.
I should've been more careful.

145
00:10:26,900 --> 00:10:27,900
No, it's fine.

146
00:10:28,300 --> 00:10:30,130
Wait, what's his name?

147
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:31,540
Cha Seok Jin.

148
00:10:32,470 --> 00:10:35,440
Chief Cha is also a judge
for this competition.

149
00:10:37,440 --> 00:10:40,180
Darn.
Why did it have to be Cheongma?

150
00:10:42,610 --> 00:10:44,350
(Ko Gi Han)

151
00:10:49,750 --> 00:10:51,760
Where on earth did he put it?

152
00:10:52,090 --> 00:10:53,460
Grandma, what are you doing?

153
00:10:54,730 --> 00:10:55,730
What?

154
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:58,030
It's nothing.

155
00:10:58,530 --> 00:11:00,500
Don't tell me
you're looking for that money.

156
00:11:00,970 --> 00:11:03,400
I am. What did you do with it?

157
00:11:03,970 --> 00:11:07,000
I knew you'd do this,
so I hid it really well.

158
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:08,240
What?

159
00:11:08,740 --> 00:11:11,080
I told you. It belongs to Eun Seol.

160
00:11:11,380 --> 00:11:13,340
So just pretend it doesn't exist.

161
00:11:14,110 --> 00:11:16,210
Then you shouldn't have shown it
to me in the first place.

162
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:19,150
I saw it with my own two eyes.
How can I pretend it doesn't exist?

163
00:11:20,450 --> 00:11:21,990
We're about to get kicked out
of this house,

164
00:11:22,050 --> 00:11:23,750
so what are we going to do?

165
00:11:24,420 --> 00:11:25,760
Come on, Eun Guk.

166
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:28,330
Let's use that money
to rent a place, okay?

167
00:11:28,890 --> 00:11:31,460
I have enough
for a security deposit,

168
00:11:31,700 --> 00:11:32,830
so don't you worry.

169
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:36,330
We can add that money
and get a better place.

170
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:37,400
That's enough.

171
00:11:37,900 --> 00:11:40,000
Stop it
and let's eat breakfast, Grandma.

172
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:41,470
- What the...
- Okay?

173
00:11:45,480 --> 00:11:47,280
Hae Ra, what time did you get
in yesterday?

174
00:11:48,450 --> 00:11:49,710
I'm not a kid anymore.

175
00:11:49,710 --> 00:11:51,950
Do you really need to monitor
when I get home?

176
00:11:52,050 --> 00:11:54,420
If you don't want me to meddle,
then get married.

177
00:11:54,690 --> 00:11:55,920
To Seok Jin?

178
00:11:57,660 --> 00:11:59,290
I'm not joking.

179
00:11:59,820 --> 00:12:01,190
Neither am I.

180
00:12:02,690 --> 00:12:04,930
Is this really necessary
so early in the morning?

181
00:12:05,360 --> 00:12:07,530
Dad, why do you hate
Seok Jin so much?

182
00:12:07,970 --> 00:12:10,430
He's been working day and night
to get on your good side.

183
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:12,240
Who said I hate him?

184
00:12:12,470 --> 00:12:14,040
I'm just saying
he's not the right match for you.

185
00:12:14,370 --> 00:12:15,370
How so?

186
00:12:15,470 --> 00:12:17,610
Because Seok Jin's family
isn't impressive enough?

187
00:12:18,110 --> 00:12:19,780
That was the case for you too.

188
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:21,350
Hae Ra.

189
00:12:21,910 --> 00:12:23,310
That's highly inappropriate.

190
00:12:24,280 --> 00:12:26,680
Unbelievable.
You really have zero filter.

191
00:12:28,420 --> 00:12:30,320
It's no use, no matter what you say.

192
00:12:30,860 --> 00:12:33,290
If you want to inherit the company,
you'll listen to me.

193
00:12:40,130 --> 00:12:43,530
This is why I didn't want Seok Jin
back in Korea.

194
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:47,100
Don't be so against it.

195
00:12:47,100 --> 00:12:48,770
Hae Ra is crazy about him,

196
00:12:48,870 --> 00:12:51,180
so at least give the guy a chance.

197
00:12:51,180 --> 00:12:52,780
What chance?

198
00:12:52,780 --> 00:12:55,480
Will it magically change
his family background...

199
00:12:55,550 --> 00:12:57,250
or grant him power he lacks?

200
00:12:57,380 --> 00:12:58,950
But the boy is smart.

201
00:12:59,050 --> 00:13:00,320
Right, and that's the problem.

202
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:02,420
Being smart
is all he has going for him.

203
00:13:02,950 --> 00:13:04,890
Kids who grow up poor but smart...

204
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:07,890
always end up greedy
with a massive inferiority complex.

205
00:13:08,430 --> 00:13:11,060
There are plenty of smart kids
from good families,

206
00:13:11,260 --> 00:13:14,470
so don't go putting ideas
in Hae Ra's head. Got it?

207
00:13:15,930 --> 00:13:17,030
I'm heading out.

208
00:13:19,700 --> 00:13:21,640
There are things you just don't say.

209
00:13:21,670 --> 00:13:23,570
What were you thinking,
saying that to the CEO?

210
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:25,510
Was I lying?

211
00:13:25,710 --> 00:13:29,850
I heard Dad's side of the family
was way poorer than Seok Jin's.

212
00:13:30,650 --> 00:13:33,020
And what do you gain from that?

213
00:13:33,750 --> 00:13:37,560
Did you expect him to roll over
and let you marry Seok Jin?

214
00:13:39,790 --> 00:13:42,230
Just be smart for once, please.

215
00:13:42,930 --> 00:13:46,300
Seok Jin's working day and night
to win the CEO's approval.

216
00:13:46,930 --> 00:13:49,630
If you can't help him,
at least don't ruin his chances.

217
00:13:50,330 --> 00:13:52,540
What are you suggesting I do?

218
00:13:52,940 --> 00:13:55,840
You need to buy Seok Jin some time.

219
00:13:56,710 --> 00:13:58,710
Time for him to win over the CEO.

220
00:14:05,680 --> 00:14:07,050
(Recovering core values,
Loss of identity)

221
00:14:07,050 --> 00:14:09,950
(Equality, Refined grace,
Timeless elegance, Rebirth)

222
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:00,570
It's Lee Jung Tae again.
What should I do?

223
00:15:02,370 --> 00:15:03,370
Don't answer it.

224
00:15:04,010 --> 00:15:05,010
Yes, ma'am.

225
00:15:08,950 --> 00:15:11,850
The person you are trying to reach
is unavailable.

226
00:15:11,920 --> 00:15:13,950
Please leave a message
after the tone.

227
00:15:24,130 --> 00:15:25,130
Is it Lee Jung Tae?

228
00:15:25,760 --> 00:15:26,760
Yes, ma'am.

229
00:15:32,470 --> 00:15:34,140
I'm not making a threat here.

230
00:15:34,540 --> 00:15:36,440
Ko Eun Seol's brother barged in,

231
00:15:36,510 --> 00:15:37,880
and I lost the cash.

232
00:15:38,140 --> 00:15:40,710
If you just give me enough
for a plane ticket back to Vietnam,

233
00:15:41,210 --> 00:15:42,710
I'll never call you again.

234
00:15:46,380 --> 00:15:47,380
What should I do?

235
00:15:48,050 --> 00:15:49,250
Just ignore him.

236
00:15:50,090 --> 00:15:51,360
Yes, understood.

237
00:15:52,820 --> 00:15:53,820
By the way...

238
00:15:55,660 --> 00:15:57,390
What is it?
Do you have something to say?

239
00:15:58,300 --> 00:16:01,130
My team is up in arms over
the open competition's PR budget...

240
00:16:01,930 --> 00:16:04,000
being set way too low.

241
00:16:05,270 --> 00:16:07,470
So how much do you need?

242
00:16:08,640 --> 00:16:11,880
They're asking for roughly
a 50 percent budget increase.

243
00:16:12,780 --> 00:16:14,180
By as much as 50 percent?

244
00:16:17,820 --> 00:16:20,520
All right. I'll see what I can do.

245
00:16:21,420 --> 00:16:22,620
Thank you, Ms. Joo.

246
00:16:22,650 --> 00:16:24,660
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

247
00:16:30,230 --> 00:16:31,560
An increase to the PR budget?

248
00:16:31,630 --> 00:16:32,630
Yes.

249
00:16:32,730 --> 00:16:35,630
The former chief was notoriously
tight with promotion funds.

250
00:16:35,900 --> 00:16:37,840
I assume this was modeled
after his old numbers.

251
00:16:37,970 --> 00:16:39,400
I'm sorry to say this.

252
00:16:39,670 --> 00:16:41,740
The budget for the second half
is already finalized,

253
00:16:41,810 --> 00:16:43,370
so that's going to be tough,
Director Joo.

254
00:16:43,710 --> 00:16:45,510
But there's such a thing
as a supplementary budget.

255
00:16:45,710 --> 00:16:47,780
Isn't this exactly
what it's meant for?

256
00:16:48,780 --> 00:16:50,110
How much do you need?

257
00:16:50,280 --> 00:16:52,020
About twice the current budget.

258
00:16:52,780 --> 00:16:54,120
That's not possible.

259
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:56,020
Even with a supplementary budget,

260
00:16:56,090 --> 00:16:59,090
I still have to be fair
to the other departments.

261
00:17:00,220 --> 00:17:02,330
Then what's the maximum
you can approve?

262
00:17:03,290 --> 00:17:05,600
I can't give you
an exact number right now,

263
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:07,300
but I'll look into it.

264
00:17:10,300 --> 00:17:13,170
Okay. Then I'll be counting on you,
Chief Cha.

265
00:17:15,040 --> 00:17:17,010
The PR team promised to work hard,

266
00:17:17,010 --> 00:17:19,940
so please give them
your full support, Chief Cha.

267
00:17:20,010 --> 00:17:21,110
As a favor to me.

268
00:17:21,810 --> 00:17:23,010
I'll get back to you on that.

269
00:17:23,680 --> 00:17:24,680
All right.

270
00:17:54,680 --> 00:17:55,780
Hey, Dad.

271
00:17:57,410 --> 00:17:58,420
Right now?

272
00:17:59,920 --> 00:18:00,980
Okay.

273
00:18:08,060 --> 00:18:11,400
Did you say Eun Guk took this
from Lee Jung Tae?

274
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:14,530
Yes. He apparently
beat the guy to a pulp...

275
00:18:14,600 --> 00:18:16,000
and took this money from him.

276
00:18:17,230 --> 00:18:18,270
Eun Guk did that?

277
00:18:19,270 --> 00:18:21,070
Your attorney dropped by recently...

278
00:18:21,070 --> 00:18:24,480
and gave us the whole speech
about you being framed.

279
00:18:26,310 --> 00:18:27,880
I guess Eun Guk was too ashamed
to face you.

280
00:18:27,980 --> 00:18:30,150
He told me to give you this
and just left.

281
00:18:31,950 --> 00:18:34,050
Anyway, this money...

282
00:18:34,690 --> 00:18:36,350
You're not going to keep it,
are you?

283
00:18:36,620 --> 00:18:37,690
Mom, not again.

284
00:18:38,060 --> 00:18:39,860
What if Eun Guk finds out?

285
00:18:39,920 --> 00:18:42,130
We can just tell him
we gave it to her.

286
00:18:42,790 --> 00:18:44,130
You'll go along with that,
won't you?

287
00:18:44,700 --> 00:18:46,060
I'm sorry, Grandma.

288
00:18:46,530 --> 00:18:49,330
I think I need to keep this money
as evidence.

289
00:18:49,830 --> 00:18:53,470
What? Evidence? You'll keep it?

290
00:18:54,170 --> 00:18:55,240
True.

291
00:18:55,470 --> 00:18:57,570
If the real killer is caught,

292
00:18:57,570 --> 00:18:59,580
this might serve as key evidence.

293
00:19:00,140 --> 00:19:02,710
Hey, can't you be honest?

294
00:19:02,910 --> 00:19:04,950
If you want the money, just say so.

295
00:19:04,950 --> 00:19:08,490
What's with this ridiculous excuse
about it being evidence?

296
00:19:11,720 --> 00:19:13,620
In any case, I can't give you
this money, Grandma.

297
00:19:14,660 --> 00:19:16,190
I knew this would happen.

298
00:19:16,790 --> 00:19:19,330
This is what you get
for taking in a stranger.

299
00:19:19,560 --> 00:19:21,500
It just proves
the old sayings are never wrong.

300
00:19:21,570 --> 00:19:23,030
Mom, please.

301
00:19:35,010 --> 00:19:36,480
So, what do you think?

302
00:19:36,680 --> 00:19:38,050
I'll think about it a little more.

303
00:19:38,720 --> 00:19:39,850
Okay. Please do.

304
00:19:42,820 --> 00:19:43,890
- Mi Rae.
- Yes?

305
00:19:44,190 --> 00:19:45,290
Eun Seol's here.

306
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:46,760
Welcome.

307
00:19:47,590 --> 00:19:49,430
I hope you've been well.

308
00:19:53,700 --> 00:19:55,430
I'm sorry about the other day.

309
00:19:56,430 --> 00:19:57,570
Don't worry about it.

310
00:19:57,730 --> 00:19:59,500
I already told Attorney Seo,

311
00:19:59,570 --> 00:20:01,070
but I would've been
just as thrown off.

312
00:20:03,070 --> 00:20:04,780
Then I'll take that
as an accepted apology.

313
00:20:05,310 --> 00:20:06,710
Mind if I drop the formalities?

314
00:20:06,940 --> 00:20:08,550
I think I'm a bit older than you.

315
00:20:09,550 --> 00:20:10,550
Of course.

316
00:20:12,950 --> 00:20:14,750
Why the sudden change?
It's a little awkward.

317
00:20:15,750 --> 00:20:18,820
Don't you know I'm direct?
For me, it's either yes or no.

318
00:20:21,430 --> 00:20:22,590
Besides, like you said,

319
00:20:23,060 --> 00:20:26,130
it'd be good for Eun Seol and me
to support each other.

320
00:20:26,860 --> 00:20:27,860
Right?

321
00:20:28,270 --> 00:20:29,270
Of course.

322
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:33,740
- All right, let's eat. Dig in.
- Go ahead.

323
00:20:36,540 --> 00:20:39,480
So, is that person from earlier
moving into the annex?

324
00:20:40,340 --> 00:20:41,750
No, she said she'd think about it.

325
00:20:42,550 --> 00:20:43,810
- Really?
- Yes.

326
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:48,020
- Mi Rae, hold on.
- Yes?

327
00:20:48,220 --> 00:20:50,120
Why not let Eun Seol stay
in your annex then?

328
00:20:50,990 --> 00:20:51,990
Attorney Seo, please.

329
00:20:53,720 --> 00:20:55,230
The annex?

330
00:20:55,630 --> 00:20:57,430
I mean, you're looking
for a tenant anyway.

331
00:20:57,690 --> 00:20:59,360
It'd be great if Eun Seol moved in.

332
00:21:00,100 --> 00:21:01,100
Right, Eun Seol?

333
00:21:01,470 --> 00:21:04,300
Thank you,
but I'll just take the thought.

334
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:06,100
I really don't want
to burden you anymore.

335
00:21:06,670 --> 00:21:08,510
Oh, come on.
You're not putting us out.

336
00:21:09,340 --> 00:21:11,010
Like my sister just said,

337
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:12,640
you should be supporting each other.

338
00:21:15,450 --> 00:21:16,850
That's true, but...

339
00:21:18,280 --> 00:21:19,950
If you're worried about
being a burden,

340
00:21:20,120 --> 00:21:21,620
just pay her
whatever rent you're paying now.

341
00:21:23,020 --> 00:21:24,520
- Right, Teun Teun?
- What?

342
00:21:25,490 --> 00:21:28,130
Sure. Do whatever you want, Uncle.

343
00:21:28,560 --> 00:21:30,660
I'm always on your side.

344
00:21:30,760 --> 00:21:32,930
Of course.
You've always got my back.

345
00:21:34,200 --> 00:21:36,300
- Go on, eat.
- Go on. You too, Teun Teun.

346
00:21:39,440 --> 00:21:40,440
What?

347
00:22:40,900 --> 00:22:41,900
Sir,

348
00:22:42,370 --> 00:22:44,940
I put this together for you to enjoy
while you listen to music.

349
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:18,900
You have such excellent,
sophisticated taste.

350
00:23:24,780 --> 00:23:25,780
This morning,

351
00:23:26,640 --> 00:23:28,980
you must've been very upset
by what Hae Ra said.

352
00:23:29,950 --> 00:23:32,280
I spoke with her
and made sure she understands.

353
00:23:38,660 --> 00:23:40,220
I'm sorry, sir.

354
00:23:40,860 --> 00:23:42,430
I overstepped my bounds, didn't I?

355
00:23:42,990 --> 00:23:44,060
I'll see myself out.

356
00:23:45,730 --> 00:23:46,730
Director Joo.

357
00:23:49,500 --> 00:23:51,470
You still have great taste.

358
00:23:53,100 --> 00:23:54,100
I'll enjoy this.

359
00:24:11,450 --> 00:24:13,660
(Cheongma)

360
00:24:13,760 --> 00:24:16,730
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

361
00:24:16,790 --> 00:24:17,790
So,

362
00:24:18,660 --> 00:24:20,860
what's the decision
regarding the PR budget increase?

363
00:24:21,930 --> 00:24:25,370
A 30 percent increase
seems to be the best we can do.

364
00:24:26,100 --> 00:24:29,070
I said we needed double,
but only 30 percent?

365
00:24:29,440 --> 00:24:32,040
You wouldn't even have that much
if I hadn't insisted.

366
00:24:32,110 --> 00:24:33,540
I hope you can understand, Ms. Joo.

367
00:24:34,210 --> 00:24:36,580
After all, this requires approval
from the CEO.

368
00:24:37,810 --> 00:24:39,180
Sure, I understand.

369
00:24:39,850 --> 00:24:41,520
Thanks for trying, Chief Cha.

370
00:24:41,590 --> 00:24:42,820
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

371
00:24:42,890 --> 00:24:44,120
Thank you for your understanding.

372
00:24:45,220 --> 00:24:48,630
It's certainly nice having a person
you can reason with in charge.

373
00:24:49,490 --> 00:24:52,560
Your predecessor was just
a nightmare to work with.

374
00:26:04,500 --> 00:26:07,140
(CEO Kang Young Hoon)

375
00:26:07,200 --> 00:26:08,240
Here.

376
00:26:08,870 --> 00:26:09,910
How's the competition going?

377
00:26:10,970 --> 00:26:12,610
Submissions will open next week...

378
00:26:12,740 --> 00:26:14,380
and will close three days later.

379
00:26:14,810 --> 00:26:16,810
I see. And the scale?

380
00:26:17,250 --> 00:26:19,780
Out of 1,243 online applicants
in the first round,

381
00:26:20,020 --> 00:26:22,850
we narrowed it down
to 100 finalists.

382
00:26:23,650 --> 00:26:26,260
We are now receiving
physical portfolios from them.

383
00:26:26,820 --> 00:26:27,820
I see.

384
00:26:28,660 --> 00:26:29,660
What's the next step?

385
00:26:30,390 --> 00:26:33,100
Team Leader Kang,
three outside judges, and I...

386
00:26:33,130 --> 00:26:34,700
will narrow the field down
to ten people.

387
00:26:35,130 --> 00:26:38,400
They'll be tasked
with making an actual garment,

388
00:26:38,500 --> 00:26:40,640
and that's how
we'll pick the final winner.

389
00:26:41,470 --> 00:26:43,740
You said it was
a blind review process.

390
00:26:44,240 --> 00:26:45,240
That's right.

391
00:26:45,340 --> 00:26:47,080
We plan to completely disregard
their background,

392
00:26:47,140 --> 00:26:48,610
evaluating only their raw skill...

393
00:26:48,610 --> 00:26:51,980
and their artistic sense
for the Cheongma identity.

394
00:26:52,550 --> 00:26:53,550
Yes, excellent.

395
00:26:54,120 --> 00:26:56,420
Be diligent and choose well.

396
00:26:57,120 --> 00:26:58,120
Understood.

397
00:27:09,400 --> 00:27:11,300
(2026 Cheongma Open Competition:
Rediscovering the Essential)

398
00:27:18,510 --> 00:27:20,340
(Classic for All)

399
00:28:05,920 --> 00:28:06,920
- Hello.
- Hello.

400
00:28:06,920 --> 00:28:08,690
Submissions close today, right?

401
00:28:08,730 --> 00:28:09,730
Yes.

402
00:28:10,030 --> 00:28:11,560
How many have
turned theirs in so far?

403
00:28:12,030 --> 00:28:13,130
Eighty-eight.

404
00:28:13,900 --> 00:28:15,000
I see we're almost done.

405
00:28:15,370 --> 00:28:17,400
After wrapping everything up,
grab dinner on this.

406
00:28:17,870 --> 00:28:19,000
Thank you, Ms. Kang.

407
00:28:19,470 --> 00:28:20,540
Thank you.

408
00:28:22,510 --> 00:28:27,480
(Cheongma Group's Open Competition
for New Designers)

409
00:28:42,060 --> 00:28:43,190
Submissions are almost closed.

410
00:28:45,260 --> 00:28:48,000
The Design Team did great work.
Let's grab dinner together.

411
00:28:48,930 --> 00:28:50,830
I already gave them my credit card.

412
00:28:51,330 --> 00:28:52,740
The only dinner you need
to worry about is with me.

413
00:28:53,670 --> 00:28:54,670
Unbelievable.

414
00:28:55,000 --> 00:28:57,070
I'll grab my purse
and meet you downstairs in the lobby.

415
00:28:57,310 --> 00:28:58,310
Okay, got it.

416
00:29:10,690 --> 00:29:11,790
Next, please.

417
00:29:14,060 --> 00:29:16,290
- Name, please?
- It's Ko Eun Seol.

418
00:29:19,700 --> 00:29:21,300
Is this based on your first draft?

419
00:29:21,600 --> 00:29:22,700
Of course.

420
00:30:48,120 --> 00:30:51,960
(A Trap Called Desire)

421
00:30:52,060 --> 00:30:54,390
The only thing that matters
is picking the right winner.

422
00:30:54,620 --> 00:30:55,890
If you like Hae Ra,

423
00:30:55,960 --> 00:30:57,430
you should be willing
to lie for her.

424
00:30:57,530 --> 00:30:58,960
But you can't even do
that one thing.

425
00:30:59,530 --> 00:31:02,000
Hae Ra thinks she's Juliet, I swear.

426
00:31:02,070 --> 00:31:05,270
The tragic heroine who died because
her parents opposed her marriage.

427
00:31:05,470 --> 00:31:07,200
You want me to live with you too?

428
00:31:07,470 --> 00:31:08,910
Is it because you don't like us?

429
00:31:09,010 --> 00:31:10,510
It's not like
this is the only house out there.

430
00:31:10,610 --> 00:31:12,140
That's no way to live your life.

431
00:31:12,480 --> 00:31:13,540
Whatever.

432
00:31:13,540 --> 00:31:15,610
I can't live with Eun Seol,
and that's final.

433
00:31:15,850 --> 00:31:17,110
- Do you know something, Seok Jin?
- What?

434
00:31:17,110 --> 00:31:18,880
Know something? What would I know?

435
00:31:19,150 --> 00:31:20,950
Who was it that you saw?
Ko Eun Seol?

436
00:31:21,120 --> 00:31:22,350
What are you going to do now?

437
00:31:22,450 --> 00:31:24,120
What else? I have to stop her.

438
00:31:25,120 --> 00:31:27,120
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
